Error [E0068]: This callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/contract_result_misuse.jet:1:68
    |
  1 | #Pre(result > 0, "result must be positive") fn add_fee(cents: Int) => Int {
    |                                                                    ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`

Error [E0144]: `result` isn't available in a `#Pre` condition
  --> tests/ui/contract_result_misuse.jet:1:6
    |
  1 | #Pre(result > 0, "result must be positive") fn add_fee(cents: Int) => Int {
    |      ^^^^^^
 Why: `result` names the return value, which only exists once the function has returned — a `#Pre` condition runs at entry, before there is one
 Fix: use `result` only in a `#Post` condition
